ow the deal is is  something that  puts up trade barriers so the bottom  line is that um  britain economically was better off  within the european union and  brexit altogether knocks a few  percentages of the  the uk economy but without the deal that  would have been even worse  so britain leaves in less than a week  parliaments  in the uk and in europe will have to  sign off on this uh  deal will the house of commons go for it  well yes it's expected to be fairly  breezy this time not the uh torturous  scenes that we have seen when when  brexit  was debated in the house of commons and  voted on in the past years  the labor opposition party says even  though it's thin  it's the alternative would be no deal so  they are voting for it so yes it expects  it  to go through parliament without any  major difficulties  thank you for that berget massa in  london
 

